{"content":[{"c":["ZANOAH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the cities “in the lowland” that was part of Judah’s inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.34","r":"Josh.15.34","rawR":"Josh.15.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.34","value":"Josh.15.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:34"},"). The inhabitants of Zanoah worked with Hanun to rebuild the Valley Gate as well as about 1,500 feet (457.2 meters) of the city wall during the restoration of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.13","r":"Neh.3.13","rawR":"Neh.3.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.13","value":"Neh.3.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.30","r":"Neh.11.30","rawR":"Neh.11.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.30","value":"Neh.11.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:30"},"). The city is probably identifiable with Zanu’a, which is located approximately 10 miles (16.1 kilometers) west of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the cities in the Judean highlands south of Hebron that was part of Judah’s inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.56","r":"Josh.15.56","rawR":"Josh.15.56","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.56","value":"Josh.15.56"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:56"},"). It was probably inhabited by the descendants of Zanoah, Jekuthiel’s son."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ZanoahPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.34","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.34","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.34"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.13","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.13","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.13"},{"anchorText":"11:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.30","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.30","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.30"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:56","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.56","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.56","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.56"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"bc16d1c5fb149d547182cf27d36e9f02835dbcc88c8816d5ef9ab004510f6849","sourceItemName":"ZanoahPlace","sourceItemOrder":29,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ZanoahPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Zanoah (Place)","title":"Zanoah (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}